      { "name": "The Blue-Stays-Behind Rule", "body": "Deep Space Blue belongs to the atmosphere: glows, particles, focus rings. It is forbidden as a text or button color, so it never competes with the two content signals.", "section": "colors" },
      { "name": "The Uppercase-Mono Label Rule", "body": "Uppercasing is reserved for JetBrains Mono micro-labels and the logotype-style hero. Prose is never uppercased, and in the personal copy it stays lowercase and casual, first person, concrete over label.", "section": "typography" },
      { "name": "The Depth-From-Background Rule", "body": "Surfaces are flat at rest. If an element needs to feel lifted, it is because it floats above scroll (fixed position), not because it is a content card. Content cards never get more than a 1px hairline.", "section": "elevation" }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep the base near-black (#09090B) with the live starfield; let depth come from the background field and 1px hairlines, not shadows.",
      "Do use the Two-Signal system exactly: gold/amber for work, cyan for personality and interaction. Pair color with label or position so it never depends on color alone.",
      "Do go oversized on the Space Grotesk display type with tight negative tracking (-0.04em); scale is the drama.",
